{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFiled from the escape analysis on marshy-chummy-coot (2399-5e49-6b28-4d59). An instrumented\nrun (a pytest plugin hard-wiring `BindingStore.is_comment_mapped` to `False` on every loaded\nmodule copy) showed the dedup suite could not observe the primary skip being disabled\nend-to-end: the differ tests seed map state via a private `_StubBindingStore`\n(`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_comment_id_map_diff.py`), while the apply tests\nseed synthetic id-bearing payloads. Each layer's test seeds the invariant the other layer is\nsupposed to establish; no single test crosses the apply-to-differ seam with a control that\nproves the assertion actually depends on `is_comment_mapped`.\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py` (fix 8d98c298fa8) got\nclose — its `test_no_reemission_after_an_acli_post_even_when_the_body_diverges` posts the real\nenvelope, records, and re-diffs one store — but it has no unrecorded-control variant and no\ninert-guard variant, so a hard-wired-False `is_comment_mapped` still cannot be distinguished\nfrom a store that was never written.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd one new test module,\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py` (test-only; no\nproduction code), that drives the WHOLE seam with a real `BindingStore` instance:\n\n1. Reuse the recorded envelope: `from .test_comment_id_acli_envelope import\n   ACLI_SUCCESS_ENVELOPE` (relative test-package imports are the established pattern —\n   `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_capability.py:20` does `from .backend_support\n   import ...`) and obtain the transport return by calling the REAL\n   `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` stubbed only at the `acli_subprocess._run_acli` seam, exactly\n   as that module's `acli_result` fixture does.\n2. Seam test: a ticket carries TWO local comments (K_posted, K_control). First\n   `_diff_comments(ticket, key, remote, binding_store=store)`\n   (`rebar_reconciler.outbound_comments._diff_comments`) emits both. Simulate the apply for\n   K_posted only via the real `dispatch_apply_phases._record_comment_id(store, entry,\n   result)`. Re-diff against the SAME store: assert K_posted is absent and K_control is\n   still emitted. The Jira-side body diverges from both local bodies, so the SECONDARY\n   body-equality skip cannot mask an inert PRIMARY id-identity skip.\n3. Inert-guard variant (encodes the \"verify by temporarily disabling the guard\" check\n   durably): monkeypatch the store instance's `is_comment_mapped` to always return `False`\n   and assert the re-diff RE-EMITS K_posted — proving the seam assertion discriminates on\n   the guard rather than passing vacuously.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py` — new test module\n  (the only change; non-goal reaffirmed: no production code, no new review criterion).\n\n## Testing\n\nThe change IS tests: happy path (recorded comment skipped on re-diff), control path\n(unrecorded comment still emitted from the same store/ticket), and the inert-guard failure\npath (forcing `is_comment_mapped` to `False` re-emits the recorded comment). During\ndevelopment the discriminating power is additionally verified RED-first by running the seam\ntest with the guard temporarily disabled and observing the failure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test posts via the real recording path (`_record_comment_id`) with the real envelope\n      fixture (obtained through the real `acli_cli_ops.add_comment`, stubbed only at\n      `_run_acli`) against a real `BindingStore`, then re-diffs with `_diff_comments` against\n      that SAME store instance — checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py`.\n- [ ] The re-diff asserts the skip engages for the recorded comment AND does not engage for\n      an unrecorded control comment — checked by the same pytest run.\n- [ ] The suite fails if `is_comment_mapped` is inert: a variant forcing it to `False`\n      asserts the recorded comment is re-emitted — checked by the same pytest run."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787443753077837001,"uuid":"f6d15835-51ab-4f9b-ae58-24863fa97f15"}